        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">picker-icon</code> CSS selector. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.14.0).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/selectors/picker-icon\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/selectors/picker-icon</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27546",
            "title": "Chrome 133 already added `::picker-icon` CSS pseudo-element",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-14T18:07:55.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-09T19:24:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">checkmark</code> CSS selector. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.14.0).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/selectors/checkmark\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/selectors/checkmark</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27545",
            "title": "Chrome 133 already added `::checkmark` CSS pseudo-element",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-14T18:08:34.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-09T19:23:11.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">WEBGL_compressed_texture_pvrtc</code> API. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.14.0).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/api/WEBGL_compressed_texture_pvrtc\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/api/WEBGL_compressed_texture_pvrtc</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27543",
            "title": "Chrome 124 added WEBGL_compressed_texture_pvrtc API",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-15T09:16:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-09T19:15:08.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96347576?u=798adeac17b0340c3666d020c6f3391d71339849&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added a sub-feature to <code class=\"notranslate\">html.elements.input.type_date</code> to indicate when browsers prevent picking dates outside the min/max range in the date picker UI.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As cited in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3026356562\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656/hovercard?comment_id=2867357979&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656#issuecomment-2867357979\">#26656 (comment)</a> .<br>\nPlease <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/caugner/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/caugner\">@caugner</a>, confirm the versions.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n \n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #26656.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3026356562\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26656\">#26656</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27450",
            "title": "Safari iOS doesn't disable invalid values in date picker UI",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-17T10:30:59.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-30T14:54:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "adi-ray",
                "url": "https://github.com/adi-ray"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36379249?u=4840c2d79361800483d4c22b03d928ae33115103&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As discussed in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18\" rel=\"nofollow\">Mozilla Bug 1316857 comment 18</a>, the concept of \"same script\" is vague and likely inaccurate.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Additionally, to determine script-closeability, browsers switched from 'has an opener' to 'was opened by script' and that might be useful to note.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316857#c18</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"834043421\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/9492\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/9492/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/9492\">#9492</a></p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My perception is these notes are usually quite short. Script-closeability also depends on the session history, so something like \"Before Chrome 95, scripts could only close windows that had an opener\" would be incorrect. I tried to omit this detail, but am unsure whether that made my phrasing too awkward. We could remove the notes entirely. An alternative phrasing might be \"Before Chrome 95, whether a window could be closed by script depended on having an opener, not on whether it was created by web content.\"</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27396",
            "title": "Chrome 95 / FF 128 add script-closeability depending on opener",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-19T07:39:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-24T14:09:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "vinhill",
                "url": "https://github.com/vinhill"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for all browsers for the <code class=\"notranslate\">global_attributes</code> SVG feature. This replaces a majority of ranges within the SVG global attributes by copying data from the CSS property counterparts.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27389",
            "title": "Update all browsers data for global_attributes SVG feature",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-15T09:30:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-23T17:33:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177243?u=702b96ad69bf6e6823b7530dad917ab8b4d9b761&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The WhatWG spec for <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#the-navigator-object\" rel=\"nofollow\">the navigator object</a> does not list these properties as deprecated, but <em>does</em> call them out as being <em>useful</em> rather than to be avoided.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">While for security reasons the <em>amount</em> of information provided by browsers through navigator properties has been reduced from what the older standard allowed for (as highlighted by the warning in the spec that \"<em>user agent implementers are strongly urged to include as little information in this API as possible</em>\", which all browsers have indeed taken to heart by only providing summary information rather than detailed information), the properties themselves have not been deprecated, and the use of <code class=\"notranslate\">navigator</code> has in no way been marked as bad. As per the text for the navigator object itself, rather the opposite:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In certain cases, despite the best efforts of the entire industry, web browsers have bugs and limitations that web authors are forced to work around.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This section defines a collection of attributes that can be used to determine, from script, the kind of user agent in use, in order to work around these issues.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#the-navigator-object\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#the-navigator-object</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#dom-navigator-vendor-dev\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#dom-navigator-vendor-dev</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#dom-navigator-platform-dev\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#dom-navigator-platform-dev</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1336781702\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/17322\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/17322/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/17322\">#17322</a> (which incorrectly marked them as deprecated in 2022, when the spec already read what it reads today)</li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1184851631\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/14429\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/14429/hovercard?comment_id=3092444674&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/14429#issuecomment-3092444674\">mdn/content#14429 (comment)</a> (link to a summary comment that tracks how this change happened, and how it probably shouldn't have)</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27342",
            "title": "Remove deprecation for navigator.vendor and navigator.platform",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-14T00:33:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-20T15:48:46.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Pomax",
                "url": "https://github.com/Pomax"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for all browsers for the <code class=\"notranslate\">text-orientation</code> CSS property. The data comes from manual testing, running test code through BrowserStack, SauceLabs, custom VMs and/or locally.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Test Code:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"\n(Using bcd.testCSSProperty() from the collector)\n\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\n(Using bcd.testCSSProperty() from the collector)\n\n</code></pre></div>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27189",
            "title": "Update all browsers data for text-orientation CSS property",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-11T16:54:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T05:02:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">speak</code> CSS property. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.13.3).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/properties/speak\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/properties/speak</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27188",
            "title": "Chrome 8 added `speak` CSS property",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-14T18:16:01.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T04:36:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Based on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1140067250\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15006\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006\">#15006</a>.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds the <code class=\"notranslate\">abort</code> event on <code class=\"notranslate\">IDBDatabase</code>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The data was originally removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1140067250\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15006\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006\">#15006</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #15345.\">Fixes</span>: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1166786936\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345\">#15345</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27167",
            "title": "Re-add IDBDatabase abort event",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-15T09:47:57.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-27T14:00:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136 adds support to the MediaRecorder API for HEVC encoding, introducing the hvc1.* codec string, and adds new codecs (hev1.* and avc3.*) supporting variable resolution video in MP4. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6375884229181440\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6375884229181440</a> for more details.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for this support to the <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder()</code> constructor, and to the <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported()</code> static method.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder.mimeType</code> property is also related, but it only returns a previously-set value rather than setting a MIME type, so I decided to not add a data point there.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
